  "id": "normalized-i8-normal",
  "description": "NORMAL as signed normalized BYTE, with -128 in two of the three vertices. That is the value \u00a73.6.2.2's max(c/127, -1) rule exists for: divided by 127 it is -1.0079, which is not a unit vector, and the vendored cgltf does not clamp it -- so this fixture is the corpus's own witness for the ClampNormalizedSigned workaround (known_bugs.md, GLTF-056). The vectors are axis-aligned because 127 is prime and no off-axis 8-bit triple decodes to unit length; an unclamped decode is 1.0079 long, which the corpus's unit-length invariant reports on its own.",
